<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Will charging a deposit scare away new clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In practice, a small, clearly-stated deposit rarely deters genuine bookings — it mainly filters out the casual, low-intent bookings that were most likely to no-show anyway. The key is communicating it plainly at the point of booking, not springing it on the client afterward."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What's a reasonable no-show rate for a Dubai salon?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most well-run salons with a deposit and reminder system in place see no-show rates in the low single digits. Salons with no system at all often run considerably higher without realising it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should the reminder come by SMS, WhatsApp, or email?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"WhatsApp consistently gets read and replied to fastest in the UAE market, and offers a two-way reply-to-confirm-or-reschedule convenience that SMS and email lack."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I introduce a deposit policy without upsetting existing regular clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Announce it clearly in advance, such as a WhatsApp broadcast or Instagram post explaining the change and why, rather than applying it silently."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a waitlist worth setting up if my salon is already usually fully booked?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — a fully booked salon is exactly where a waitlist pays off most, because every cancellation that goes unfilled is a guaranteed loss rather than a maybe."}}]}</script>

			
			
